#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0249.1 expect=noViolation domain=BW
#note "EMPTY-DATASET PIN, re-noted under PLAN-zero-row-routing-rekey.md (owner rulings Q1 / Q5 / 6c-1, Fix #349 / EC-89; policy text: lib/corej-cdisc-rules/documentation/zero-row-policy.md). BW declared with DOMAIN and STUDYID, zero rows. Ruled: a row-reading rule has nothing to check on an empty dataset -> EXECUTED, 0 findings, never SKIPPED. var_exists(\"DOMAIN\") is TRUE on the real metadata (the retired synthetic zero-column table was the only reason it was ever false here), and is_inconsistent_across_dataset(STUDYID, keys=[DOMAIN]) has no row to group over the real 0-row table. The empty BW is reported once, by CDISC-SEND-0278."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset BW label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
---
